    {
      "type": "container",
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "class": "columns"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "element",
          "tag": "p",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "section-label"
          },
          "html": "The details"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "section-title"
          },
          "html": "Two philosophies of driving the AI."
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "tag": "p",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "section-sub"
          },
          "html": "The generator is the AI. The differentiator is who writes the prompt."
        },
        {
          "type": "cards",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "columns-grid"
          },
          "prefix": "",
          "suffix": "",
          "items": [
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "col-card highlight"
              },
              "html": "\n                <p class=\"col-sub\">Caresse</p>\n                <h3>Listen without giving anything. The team did the work.</h3>\n                <p>Before you even consider paying, you get access to pre-generated audio demos in English, French and Spanish. No sign-up, no email, no account. You hear right away the sound quality, the voice, and the intensity levels.</p>\n                <p>On the AI approach itself, Caresse starts from one observation: on territory as delicate as intimacy, you don't want to formulate what you want to the AI. So all the prompt-engineering work is done upstream by the Caresse team. Each pipeline phase (setup, immersion, first touches, exploration, intensity crescendo, polishing) has its dedicated prompt, tested and refined. You just configure your profile — like filling out a confidential form. The pipeline does the rest. Anonymous mode needs no Caresse account; purchases use your Apple or Google account.</p>\n                <ul>\n                    <li>Free audio demos, no sign-up at all (EN · FR · ES)</li>\n                    <li>Anonymous mode without a Caresse account; purchases use your Apple or Google account</li>\n                    <li>Prompts written and refined by the Caresse editorial team</li>\n                    <li>Multi-phase pipeline to guarantee narrative pacing</li>\n                    <li>Form-based configuration (no chat to formulate)</li>\n                    <li>Duration varies with generation; exact length is not a setting</li>\n                    <li>Voice synthesized via premium TTS</li>\n                </ul>\n            "
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "col-card muted"
              },
              "html": "\n                <p class=\"col-sub\">InTheMoment</p>\n                <h3>The user describes, the AI picks the technique.</h3>\n                <p>InTheMoment takes the modern AI approach: you describe your situation to the AI in a few words, it picks from a wide catalog of established meditation and hypnosis techniques, then generates an adapted session. You can configure voice, length, posture, preferred technique.</p>\n                <p>Effective, and the \"pick from established techniques\" safeguard keeps the AI from going off the rails. Designed for a use case different from ours — personal wellness — where free-form conversation makes sense.</p>\n                <ul>\n                    <li>Generation from user description</li>\n                    <li>Catalog of meditation/hypnosis techniques</li>\n                    <li>Voice, posture, technique configuration</li>\n                    <li>Free plan (2 sessions/day) + Pro</li>\n                    <li>9 languages on Pro plan</li>\n                </ul>\n            "
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "container",
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "class": "quality"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "element",
          "tag": "p",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "section-label"
          },
          "html": "Why it changes everything"
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "section-title"
          },
          "html": "AI without a curated prompt is fine. With one, it's right."
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "tag": "p",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "section-sub"
          },
          "html": "On intimate ground, the difference between \"fine\" and \"right\" is everything."
        },
        {
          "type": "container",
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "quality-card"
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "element",
              "tag": "h3",
              "attrs": {},
              "html": "The 6-phase Caresse pipeline"
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "html": "A Caresse session isn't generated in one shot. It runs through six successive phases, each with its dedicated prompt, written for its role in the narrative arc: setup, immerse, open, explore, crescendo, polish. Each prompt is versioned, tested, refined, with specific variants for couple mode and solo mode."
            },
            {
              "type": "element",
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "html": "Why this much care? Because on intimate ground, a generic prompt produces flat narration, without rhythm, that pulls you out of the scene instead of pulling you in. The Caresse team spent months tuning the warmth of the voice, the cadence, the exact moment intensity rises. You see none of this machinery — you just live a session that sounds right."
            },
            {
              "type": "container",
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "phases"
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "html": "\n                "
                },
                {
